Package: PleioMatchR
Type: Package
Title: Diagnostic Tools for Cross-Trait GWAS Sharing
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R: person("PleioMatchR", "Developers",
    email = "pleiomatchr.developers@example.com",
    role = c("aut", "cre"))
Description: A matched-control, permutation-based framework for
    diagnosing whether a predefined set of trait-associated loci shows
    association enrichment, consistent effect direction, or
    pathway-stratified sharing in a second genome-wide association study
    (GWAS).  The package implements control-pool construction with
    chromosome, minor-allele-frequency, physical-distance and optional
    LD-score stratification; shared-control paired permutation tests for
    enrichment; sign-flip direction tests and weighted direction
    diagnostics; cross-ancestry allele-frequency drift checks; and
    base-graphics visualisation ('butterfly', null-distribution and
    forest plots).  All results are association-level diagnostics and do
    not imply causal relationships.
